{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RgmVndv4a8LRKVKiwLVvJH","type":"tool_result","content":"=== handwritten diff\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\nindex 8c4dde7e4..195a2d213 100644\n--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -35,12 +35,14 @@ You need [Deno 2.9+](https://docs.deno.com/runtime/getting_started/installation/\n \n ```bash\n # 1. Install the NetScript CLI on your PATH\n-deno install --global --allow-all --name netscript jsr:@netscript/cli@<version>\n+deno install --global --allow-all --name netscript --minimum-dependency-age=0 jsr:@netscript/cli@<version>\n \n # 2. Scaffold a workspace: contracts + a typed example service + Postgres + Aspire orchestration\n netscript init my-app --db postgres --service --yes\n ```\n \n+Deno 2.9 refuses packages published in the last 24 hours by default; `--minimum-dependency-age=0` lets a same-day release install.\n+\n Replace `<version>` with the current release — the\n [latest tag](https://github.com/rickylabs/netscript/releases/latest), or the version shown on\n [jsr.io/@netscript/cli](https://jsr.io/@netscript/cli). Bare `jsr:@netscript/*` specifiers do not\ndiff --git a/docs/site/quickstart.vto b/docs/site/quickstart.vto\nindex 11f7f46ef..84991256c 100644\n--- a/docs/site/quickstart.vto\n+++ b/docs/site/quickstart.vto\n@@ -20,13 +20,13 @@ the local orchestrator; your application code remains Deno and TypeScript. See\n <!-- quickstart-walk:start -->\n \n ```bash\n-deno install --global --allow-all --name netscript jsr:@netscript/cli{{ releaseSpecifier }}\n+deno install --global --allow-all --name netscript --minimum-dependency-age=0 jsr:@netscript/cli{{ releaseSpecifier }}\n ```\n \n The same command works in Bash and PowerShell; Deno prints the executable directory to add to `PATH` if `netscript` is not found.\n \n {{ comp callout { type: \"note\", title: \"Installing on a release day or a canary\" } }}\n-Deno refuses dependencies published in the last ~24 hours, so on the day a version ships the command above fails. Add <code>--minimum-dependency-age=0</code> to override the policy, and <code>-f</code> to replace an existing global executable:\n+Deno refuses dependencies published in the last ~24 hours by default; the command above already overrides that policy. Add <code>-f</code> only to replace an existing global executable:\n <code>deno install -g -A -f -n netscript --minimum-dependency-age=0 jsr:@netscript/cli{{ releaseSpecifier }}</code>\n {{ /comp }}\n \ndiff --git a/packages/cli/README.md b/packages/cli/README.md\nindex e90cc55f0..62412f9e0 100644\n--- a/packages/cli/README.md\n+++ b/packages/cli/README.md\n@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@ flowchart LR\n ## Install\n \n ```bash\n-deno install --global --allow-all --name netscript jsr:@netscript/cli@<version>\n+deno install --global --allow-all --name netscript --minimum-dependency-age=0 jsr:@netscript/cli@<version>\n ```\n \n Or as a library, for the embeddable command tree:\ndiff --git a/packages/cli/e2e/src/domain/readme-quickstart.ts b/packages/cli/e2e/src/domain/readme-quickstart.ts\nindex fda9997ac..e771b6f40 100644\n--- a/packages/cli/e2e/src/domain/readme-quickstart.ts\n+++ b/packages/cli/e2e/src/domain/readme-quickstart.ts\n@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@ export interface ReadmeQuickstartSubstitutions {\n \n /** Ordered command contract expected by the `readme.quickstart` suite. */\n export const README_QUICKSTART_EXPECTED_COMMANDS = [\n-  'deno install --global --allow-all --name netscript jsr:@netscript/cli@<version>',\n+  'deno install --global --allow-all --name netscript --minimum-dependency-age=0 jsr:@netscript/cli@<version>',\n   'netscript init my-app --db postgres --service --yes',\n   'cd my-app/aspire',\n   'aspire restore',\ndiff --git a/packages/cli/e2e/suites/quickstart/quickstart-walk-suite.ts b/packages/cli/e2e/suites/quickstart/quickstart-walk-suite.ts\nindex 518949e0f..b10ed3ae4 100644\n--- a/packages/cli/e2e/suites/quickstart/quickstart-walk-suite.ts\n+++ b/packages/cli/e2e/suites/quic